; Frozen interface F10: out-of-process module/adapter wire (aegis-adapter-host <-> third-party module).
; Transport: SOCK_SEQPACKET UDS, one frame per message, postcard-encoded per the WIT package aegis:data@0.1.0;
; this CDDL is the normative shape (postcard is a positional encoding of the same structures).
; Host-side decoders of module output are in the verified TCB (SPEC_INVARIANTS §H): every frame is length-capped
; (64 KiB default), fully validated before use, and a decode failure kills the module (crash budget), never the host.

frame      = request / response
request    = [0, req-id, op]            ; op = the checked F4 Op, tenant already bound by the host
response   = [1, req-id, result]
req-id     = uint .size 8
result     = [0, rows] / [1, error-code]
rows       = [* row]
row        = [* value / null]
value      = int / tstr
error-code = 1..255                      ; uniform codes; no existence oracle (W6)
op         = [tenant: uint .gt 0, collection: tstr, kind: 0..4, filter: pred, writes: [* [uint, value]], returning: [* uint]]
pred       = [0] / [1] / [2, uint, value] / [3, uint, [* value]] / [4, uint, value, value] / [5, uint, tstr]
           / [6, pred, pred] / [7, pred, pred] / [8, pred]    ; tt ff eq isIn range pfx and or not (Lowering.lean)
; Shapes above unchanged by the P4-spec-001 re-freeze (F4 Op/Pred layout kept). Normative notes added with it:
; - kind code i is OpKind::ALL[i] (select insert update delete upsert) and owns bit 1<<i of an F4 OpMask.
; - tenant is the raw u64; a module renders it only as F4 tenant_text (16 lower-case hex digits) in SQL text
;   columns, or as the F4 kv_key_prefix t:{<16 hex>}: in Redis/Valkey keys (decision D4). No other encoding.
; - the host runs F4 authorize (CapSet) and check_schema before sending a request; a module never sees an op
;   its route was not granted. Emitting an F4 denylist item to the engine breaks the extension contract
;   (SPEC_INVARIANTS H); the host does not see an out-of-process module's engine traffic, so this is a contract
;   term, not a host check.
; P8-spec-001 (normative note only, shapes unchanged): the F4 denylist a module must honour is per engine family and
;   includes `mariadb` (SPEC_INVARIANTS F, Phase-8 addendum DENY-M: its keyword items and lexical forms, e.g. user
;   variables, multi-statements, executable comments, unguarded ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE).
